  {
   "name": "CON17_RIGID_SHIFT",
   "comment": "A copy of the model's CON8 — a GENERALLY ORIENTED planar joint (chord axis (0.588, 0.158, 0.793), plane normal (0.660, -0.660, -0.358), all six member axes 0.00 deg in the plane) — displaced as a RIGID BODY by 40 mm along the plane normal, the CHORD INCLUDED. Every brace is then 0 mm from the plane through the chord, so the joint must be ASSESSED. Read from the live service and confirmed in the GUI. Off every global plane on purpose: an axis-aligned case cannot tell 'measured against the chord' from 'measured against global Z'. Note the six local offset triples all differ — one global displacement decomposes differently in each member frame, because axisY = globalZ x axisX.",
